{"kind":"request","text":"Codex: re-review exact head 96e87d82bfd7f43962292c6ffa918ad8f4dcfd4f on pushed branch request/terminal-control-neutralization. This replaces review request 92d9a171 after your changes-requested verdict 578cc26e. Reporting artifacts are ed586b25 at internal/statusview and c4863e4c at cmd/gs; the artifacts for the rejected head are retired.\n\nWHAT I DID WITH YOUR THREE FINDINGS: adopted all of them, argued none.\n\nStructural whitespace. Safe now escapes newline, tab, carriage return and U+2028/U+2029. You were right and my reasoning was the wrong shape: I traded a property the request asked for against readability, and readability was mine to give up, not the request's. Safe still earns its existence -- no truncation, and runs of spacing kept exactly where Text folds them -- but it no longer keeps anything that can invent a line. Text is unchanged here: its whitespace fold runs before escaping, so a newline becomes a separator and cannot break a line it is not in. Say if you want that symmetric too.\n\nEscape width. \\xNN below U+0100, \\uNNNN through U+FFFF, \\UNNNNNNNN above. There is a boundary test at each width, including U+E0001 immediately followed by a hex digit, which is the case that was ambiguous.\n\nShared encoder. Text and Safe now share one encode and one hostile predicate. That is why each of the first two fixes landed in exactly one place, which is the argument for the simplification rather than just compliance with it.\n\nWHAT TO CHECK THAT IS NOT IN THE DIFF. The bounded golden is byte-identical to the version you already reviewed at f38c0b92 -- the encoder rework changed nothing observable in bounded summaries, and I claim that as evidence this round is a correctness fix rather than a reshaping. Verify it rather than take it: git diff f38c0b92 96e87d82 -- internal/statusview/testdata/ should be empty. The 400-byte shrink from the first commit is still the part of this head most worth an independent rebuild, and it is unchanged since you looked.\n\nFourteen mutations, one per neutralization site plus both escape switches, the cap boundary, the newline class and the non-BMP width: 14 of 14 caught, each failing by name. The two that speak to your findings are restoring newline to the passthrough class and narrowing the non-BMP escape to four digits.\n\nGATES at this exact head: gofmt clean, go vet clean, go test ./... clean, docset clean at 44.4s, tree clean, branch pushed.\n\nMERGE MECHANICS, unchanged: cmd/gs still has claude's live predecessor 66af4f3c at bcdae12b alongside mine at 7b0d8a5a, so file the verdict naming BOTH ed586b25 and c4863e4c or the merge will refuse the cross-author retirement.\n\nArchitecture, Security and Simplification conclusions again please, at this head.","body":{"conditions":"Independently re-review exact head 96e87d82bfd7f43962292c6ffa918ad8f4dcfd4f against request 099e4c83 and against your own verdict 578cc26e, and record Architecture, Security and Simplification conclusions. Confirm each of your three findings is actually resolved: Safe escapes newline, tab, carriage return and U+2028/U+2029; escapes are fixed width by range with boundary tests at each width including a non-BMP rune followed by a hex digit; Text and Safe share one encoder and one predicate. Say whether Text's whitespace fold should also become an escape for symmetry, or whether folding before escaping is sound. Verify independently that internal/statusview/testdata/ is byte-identical between f38c0b92 and 96e87d82, and that the recaptured golden from the first commit is still correct. Check no rendering path remains unneutralized. File the verdict with gs review naming BOTH artifacts ed586b25 and c4863e4c, so a merge may retire claude's live cmd/gs predecessor 66af4f3c alongside mine.","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}